@@OLD
  # read, because library functions run under an explicit `bash`; LANG and the
  # locale categories change no record either: the harness runs under the
  # caller's locale, pins `LC_ALL=C` at the sites where collation actually
  # matters, and fails closed in a locale that cannot decode the kit's bytes
  # (Shift-JIS, or a UTF-8 locale over an invalid byte; T030o42 review), while
  # a check whose programs read the locale pins it or declares it; TMPDIR
  # decides where temporary files are written, never what a check concludes.
@@NEW
  # read, because library functions run under an explicit `bash`; LANG and the
  # locale categories change no record either: the harness runs its own
  # parsing under `LC_ALL=C` (vf_locale_pin above), which decodes every byte
  # and reads every ASCII grammar the kit writes as any other locale would,
  # and gives the caller's LC_ALL back to the command a capture runs, while a
  # check whose programs read the locale pins it or declares it (O-017); TMPDIR
  # decides where temporary files are written, never what a check concludes.
@@END
